{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom collections import Counter\n\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all elements that occur more than once from a list of integers,\n    preserving the order of the remaining unique elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    # First pass: count frequencies of all elements.\n    frequency_map = Counter(numbers)\n\n    # Second pass: build the result list, keeping only elements with count 1.\n    result = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if frequency_map[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
