{"task_id": "HumanEval/31", "solution": "```python\ndef is_prime(n):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a prime number.\n    Uses an optimized trial division method for efficiency.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n <= 3:  # 2 and 3 are prime\n        return True\n\n    # Check if n is divisible by 2 or 3\n    if n % 2 == 0 or n % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for divisors from 5 up to sqrt(n)\n    # Optimized loop: check i and i+2 (all primes > 3 are of form 6k \u00b1 1)\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0 or n % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n\n    return True\n```"}
