{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts elements at indices divisible by three in a list, keeping other elements in original positions.\n    Returns a new list with the specified sorting applied.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = l[:]  # Create a shallow copy to avoid modifying the original list\n\n    # Collect elements at indices divisible by three\n    elements_to_sort = []\n    indices_to_sort = []\n    for i, item in enumerate(l):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(item)\n            indices_to_sort.append(i)\n\n    # Sort the collected elements\n    sorted_elements = sorted(elements_to_sort)\n\n    # Place sorted elements back into the result list\n    for i, sorted_item in zip(indices_to_sort, sorted_elements):\n        result_list[i] = sorted_item\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    >>> sort_third([1, 2, 3])\n    [1, 2, 3]\n    >>> sort_third([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2])\n    [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n    \"\"\"\n    indices_to_sort = []\n    values_to_sort = []\n\n    # Identify indices and extract values.\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            indices_to_sort.append(i)\n            values_to_sort.append(l[i])\n\n    # Sort the extracted values.\n    values_to_sort.sort()\n\n    # Create a copy of the original list to modify.\n    result_list = list(l)\n\n    # Place sorted values back into the result list.\n    for i, original_index in enumerate(indices_to_sort):\n        result_list[original_index] = values_to_sort[i]\n\n    return result_list\n```"}
