{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    Calculates the sum of coeff * x^i for each coefficient at index i.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a single real zero of a polynomial given its coefficients.\n    Uses bisection method after finding an initial bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_TOLERANCE = 1e-6\n    MAX_ITERATIONS = 100\n    SEARCH_RANGE_MIN = -100.0\n    SEARCH_RANGE_MAX = 100.0\n    SEARCH_STEP = 1.0\n\n    def _poly_func(x_val: float) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Helper to evaluate the polynomial with current coefficients.\"\"\"\n        return poly(xs, x_val)\n\n    def _find_bracket(func, min_val, max_val, step):\n        \"\"\"\n        Searches for an interval [a, b] where func(a) and func(b) have opposite signs.\n        Also handles cases where a root is found exactly on a step point.\n        \"\"\"\n        x1 = min_val\n        while x1 < max_val:\n            x2 = x1 + step\n            y1 = func(x1)\n            y2 = func(x2)\n\n            if y1 * y2 < 0:\n                return x1, x2\n\n            if abs(y1) < DEFAULT_TOLERANCE:\n                return x1, x1 + 0.0001\n            if abs(y2) < DEFAULT_TOLERANCE:\n                return x2, x2 + 0.0001\n\n            x1 = x2\n\n        # As per the problem's guarantee of a solution and the constraint against\n        # raising exceptions for edge cases, this part of the code should ideally\n        # not be reached under valid operating conditions and parameters.\n        # The design implies a bracket will always be found. For code execution,\n        # we provide a fallback that will be processed by bisection.\n        return min_val, max_val\n\n\n    def _bisection_method(func, a, b, tol, max_iter):\n        \"\"\"\n        Implements the bisection method to find a root of func within the interval [a, b].\n        Assumes the initial interval [a,b] brackets a root or contains one at an endpoint.\n        \"\"\"\n        # The design's explicit `NoRootFoundError` for `func(a) * func(b) > 0`\n        # is omitted due to the critical requirement against raising exceptions.\n\n        for _ in range(max_iter):\n            c = (a + b) / 2\n            y_c = func(c)\n\n            if abs(y_c) < tol:\n                return c\n\n            y_a = func(a)\n            if y_a * y_c < 0:\n                b = c\n            else:\n                a = c\n\n        # If max iterations are reached, return the current best approximation.\n        # The design's `NoRootFoundError` for non-convergence is omitted.\n        return (a + b) / 2\n\n    a, b = _find_bracket(_poly_func, SEARCH_RANGE_MIN, SEARCH_RANGE_MAX, SEARCH_STEP)\n    return _bisection_method(_poly_func, a, b, DEFAULT_TOLERANCE, MAX_ITERATIONS)\n```\n"}
