{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "```python\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    It returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Skip duplicate elements for the first pointer to optimize\n        if i > 0 and sorted_numbers[i] == sorted_numbers[i-1]:\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = sorted_numbers[i] + sorted_numbers[left] + sorted_numbers[right]\n\n            if current_sum == 0:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < 0:\n                left += 1\n            else: # current_sum > 0\n                right -= 1\n    return False\n```"}
