{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the list with the first four Fib4 numbers [fib4(n-4), fib4(n-3), fib4(n-2), fib4(n-1)]\n    # For n=4, this means [fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)]\n    fib4_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib4 = sum(fib4_sequence)\n        # Shift elements: remove the oldest and add the newest to maintain a window of the last four values.\n        fib4_sequence.pop(0)\n        fib4_sequence.append(next_fib4)\n\n    return fib4_sequence[3]"}
