{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting each lowercase English letter 5 positions backward,\n    wrapping around from 'a' to 'z'.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        # Calculate 0-indexed position, apply backward shift, and ensure wrap-around.\n        char_code = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        decoded_code = (char_code - 5 + 26) % 26\n        decoded_char = chr(decoded_code + ord('a'))\n        decoded_chars.append(decoded_char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
