{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting each lowercase English character backward by 5 positions,\n    wrapping around from 'a' to 'z'.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            # Calculate the 0-indexed position of the character from 'a'\n            char_offset = ord(char) - ord('a')\n\n            # Shift backward by 5, adding 26 to handle negative results before modulo\n            shifted_offset = (char_offset - 5 + 26) % 26\n\n            # Convert the shifted offset back to its ASCII value and then to a character\n            decoded_char_code = shifted_offset + ord('a')\n            decoded_chars.append(chr(decoded_char_code))\n        else:\n            # Non-lowercase English alphabet characters are left unchanged\n            decoded_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)\n```"}
