{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"<<><>>\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"><<>\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == '>':\n            balance -= 1\n        # If balance drops below zero, a closing bracket appeared before its opening counterpart.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n    # For correct bracketing, the final balance must be zero.\n    return balance == 0\n```"}
