{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x: int, shift: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string. If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    \"\"\"\n    x_str = str(abs(x))\n    num_digits = len(x_str)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return x_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        shifted_str = x_str[num_digits - shift:] + x_str[:num_digits - shift]\n        return shifted_str\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 1)\n    \"21\"\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 2)\n    \"12\"\n    \"\"\"\n    string_x = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(string_x)\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return string_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        return string_x[-effective_shift:] + string_x[:-effective_shift]\n```"}
