{"task_id": "HumanEval/82", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef prime_length(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the length of the input string is a prime number.\n    A prime number is a natural number greater than 1 that has no positive divisors other than 1 and itself.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a given integer n is a prime number.\n        Numbers less than 2 are not considered prime.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    length = len(string)\n    return _is_prime(length)\n```"}
