{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "def is_bored(S: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of boredoms in a string. A boredom is a sentence that starts with the word \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n    import re\n\n    boredom_count = 0\n\n    # Split the input text into potential sentences using regular expression\n    # This handles multiple delimiters and produces parts that may need trimming or filtering.\n    potential_sentences = re.split(r'[.?!]', S)\n\n    sentences = []\n    for s_part in potential_sentences:\n        trimmed_s_part = s_part.strip()\n        if trimmed_s_part:  # Ensure the sentence part is not empty after trimming\n            sentences.append(trimmed_s_part)\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        # Extract the first word from the current sentence\n        trimmed_sentence = sentence.strip()\n        first_word = None\n        if trimmed_sentence:\n            # Use regex to split by one or more whitespace characters\n            words = re.split(r'\\s+', trimmed_sentence)\n            if words:\n                first_word = words[0]\n\n        # Check if the first word exists and is \"I\" (case-insensitive)\n        if first_word and first_word.lower() == \"i\":\n            boredom_count += 1\n\n    return boredom_count"}
