{"task_id": "HumanEval/103", "solution": "```python\ndef rounded_avg(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Computes the rounded average of integers from n to m (inclusive) and returns it as a binary string.\n    Returns -1 if n > m.\"\"\"\n    if n > m:\n        return -1\n\n    # Calculate the sum of integers from n to m using the arithmetic series formula.\n    count = m - n + 1\n    total_sum = (count * (n + m)) // 2\n\n    # Compute the floating-point average.\n    average = total_sum / count\n\n    # Round the average to the nearest integer (Python's round() rounds half to even).\n    rounded_int_average = round(average)\n\n    # Convert the rounded integer to its binary string representation.\n    return bin(rounded_int_average)\n```"}
