{"task_id": "HumanEval/119", "solution": "```python\ndef match_parens(lst):\n    '''\n    Checks if two parenthesis strings can be concatenated to form a balanced string.\n    Returns 'Yes' if a balanced string can be formed, 'No' otherwise.\n    '''\n\n    def _is_balanced(s: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single string of parentheses is balanced.\"\"\"\n        balance_counter = 0\n        for char in s:\n            if char == '(':\n                balance_counter += 1\n            elif char == ')':\n                balance_counter -= 1\n            if balance_counter < 0:\n                return False\n        return balance_counter == 0\n\n    s1, s2 = lst[0], lst[1]\n\n    # Check s1 + s2 concatenation\n    if _is_balanced(s1 + s2):\n        return 'Yes'\n\n    # Check s2 + s1 concatenation\n    if _is_balanced(s2 + s1):\n        return 'Yes'\n\n    return 'No'\n```\n"}
