{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "```python\ndef check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the last character of a given string is an alphabetical character\n    and is not a part of a word. A \"word\" is a group of characters separated by space.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not txt:\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    # Check if the alphabetical last character is isolated.\n    # It is isolated if it's the only character, or the character before it is a space.\n    if len(txt) == 1:\n        return True\n    else:\n        char_before_last = txt[-2]\n        return char_before_last == ' '\n```"}
