{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "```python\ndef is_nested(string: str) -> bool:\n    '''\n    Create a function that takes a string as input which contains only square brackets.\n    The function should return True if and only if there is a valid subsequence of brackets\n    where at least one bracket in the subsequence is nested.\n\n    is_nested('[[]]') \u279e True\n    is_nested('[]]]]]]][[[[[]') \u279e False\n    is_nested('[][]') \u279e False\n    is_nested('[]') \u279e False\n    is_nested('[[][]]') \u279e True\n    is_nested('[[]][[') \u279e True\n    '''\n    class InvalidBracketStringError(ValueError):\n        \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid bracket strings.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    # Input validation as per design\n    if not isinstance(string, str):\n        raise InvalidBracketStringError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not string:\n        # According to the design, an empty string should raise an error.\n        # However, the test case `assert BracketCheckerCore.is_nested('') is False`\n        # implies that an empty string should return False if validation allows it.\n        # Reconciling this: if validation is meant to occur first, an empty string\n        # should raise an error as per the design's `validate_bracket_string`.\n        # The prompt examples do not include an empty string.\n        # Following the strict FR1 precondition and error handling: raise error for empty.\n        raise InvalidBracketStringError(\"Input string cannot be empty.\")\n    for char in string:\n        if char not in ['[', ']']:\n            raise InvalidBracketStringError(f\"Invalid character '{char}' found in string. Only '[' and ']' are allowed.\")\n\n    # Helper function to check if a substring is a valid bracket sequence\n    # A valid bracket sequence is like `[]`, `[][]`, `[[]]`\n    def _is_valid_sequence(sub_s: str) -> bool:\n        if not sub_s:\n            return False  # An empty inner sequence does not constitute nesting as per definition [A] where A is non-empty.\n\n        balance = 0\n        for char_inner in sub_s:\n            if char_inner == '[':\n                balance += 1\n            elif char_inner == ']':\n                balance -= 1\n            if balance < 0:\n                return False\n        return balance == 0\n\n    n = len(string)\n    for i in range(n):\n        if string[i] == '[':\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                if string[j] == ']':\n                    # Found a potential outer pair string[i...j]\n                    inner_sequence = string[i+1:j]\n                    if _is_valid_sequence(inner_sequence):\n                        return True  # Found a nested structure: [A] where A is a valid, non-empty bracket sequence\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/135", "solution": "```python\ndef can_arrange(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the largest index i where arr[i] is strictly less than arr[i-1].\n    If no such index exists, it returns -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return -1\n\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, 0, -1):\n        if arr[i] < arr[i - 1]:\n            return i\n\n    return -1\n```"}
