{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    in the list that are odd. Ignore numbers that are negative or not integers.\n\n    double_the_difference([1, 3, 2, 0]) == 1 + 9 + 0 + 0 = 10\n    double_the_difference([-1, -2, 0]) == 0\n    double_the_difference([9, -2]) == 81\n    double_the_difference([0]) == 0\n\n    If the input list is empty, return 0.\n    '''\n    total_sum_of_squares = 0\n\n    if not lst:\n        return 0\n\n    for item in lst:\n        # Ignore numbers that are not strictly integers (e.g., 1.5, 3.0).\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            # Only consider positive numbers.\n            if item > 0:\n                # Only consider odd numbers among the positive integers.\n                if item % 2 != 0:\n                    total_sum_of_squares += item * item\n    return total_sum_of_squares\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/154", "solution": "```python\ndef _generate_rotations(s: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Generates all unique cyclic rotations of a string.\"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return [\"\"]\n\n    rotations = set()\n    n = len(s)\n    for i in range(n):\n        rotated_s = s[i:] + s[:i]\n        rotations.add(rotated_s)\n    return sorted(list(rotations))\n\n\ndef cycpattern_check(a , b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the second word or any of its rotations is a substring in the first word.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not b:\n        return True\n\n    if not a:\n        return False\n\n    rotations_of_b = _generate_rotations(b)\n    for rotation in rotations_of_b:\n        if rotation in a:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
